1. Chatbots and tools using artificial intelligence may rely on third-party AI Services. The Licensee agrees to comply with the terms of those services.
2. Responses generated by AI may contain errors or inaccuracies. The Licensor does not guarantee their correctness, completeness or fitness for any particular purpose.
3. The Licensee is responsible for informing end users that they are interacting with an AI system, and for ensuring the deployment complies with applicable law, including rules on transparency of AI systems.
4. Chatbots must not be used autonomously to make decisions with significant legal, medical or financial effects on individuals without human oversight.
5. Costs of using AI Services (e.g. token fees, API keys) are borne by the Licensee, unless the Main Agreement provides otherwise.

